# BetterSolano — build-time configuration template
#
# Copy to .env and adjust before running `npm run build` or `npm run package`.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is git-ignored and is NEVER copied into dist/ or into the release
# archive — these values are consumed while building, not served to browsers.
# There are no server-side secrets in this project: the site is fully static,
# so anything that reaches the browser is public by definition. Do not put
# credentials here expecting them to stay private.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical site URL
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by the React app build (react-app/next.config.js) for absolute URLs.
# No trailing slash. Change this for a staging subdomain deploy.
SITE_URL=https://bettersolano.org


# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not templated — change these in source if you fork the site
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are embedded directly in the HTML rather than injected at build time,
# because the site ships as plain static pages with no templating step. They are
# listed here so a new deployment knows what is baked in and where to change it.
#
#   Google Analytics measurement ID .... G-8777S9SP9X
#     Appears in the <head> of index.html, 403.html, 404.html, 500.html and
#     every page under services/ and service-details/.
#     Find with:  grep -rl "G-8777S9SP9X" --include="*.html" .
#     A staging deploy that leaves this in place will report its traffic into
#     the production analytics property.
#
#   Facebook page ............. facebook.com/OfficialLguSolanoFanpage
#   Contact address ........... volunteer@bettersolano.org
#
# The Content-Security-Policy in .htaccess allow-lists the third-party origins
# these depend on. If you point them somewhere new, update the CSP to match or
# the browser will block them.
